# Multi-target actives for the enriched ligand-based benchmark (docs/LBVS.md).
#
# Every molecule here is an *active* because it is documented to be one, not
# because a model said so:
#
#   * `trypsin`     — benzamidine is the co-crystallised ligand of 3PTB (code BEN),
#                     and the four substituted analogues plus benzylamidine are
#                     the congeneric series demo/library.smi ships as a
#                     structure-activity set;
#   * `eralpha`     — 4-hydroxytamoxifen (OHT) and estradiol (EST) are the
#                     co-crystallised ligands of 3ERT and 1ERE_A;
#   * `hiv_protease`— XK263 (XK2) is the co-crystallised ligand of 1HVR;
#   * `egfr`        — erlotinib (AQ4) is the co-crystallised ligand of 1M17;
#   * `streptavidin`— biotin (BTN) is the co-crystallised ligand of 1STP.
#
# The four ligands whose structure file is bundled in tests/data are written out
# from that file (tests/data/BTN.sdf, EST.sdf, OHT.sdf, XK2.sdf).  Erlotinib has no
# bundled file, so it is written from the published structure and checked in
# tests/test_lbvs.py against its molecular formula (C22H23N3O4) and the 29 heavy
# atoms the 1M17 file actually contains.  Two ligands were deliberately left out:
#
#   * ritonavir, the co-crystallised ligand of 1HXW (RIT): a hand-written SMILES
#     did not reproduce C37H48N6O5S2, and deriving the bond orders from the
#     coordinates fails on every ligand in tests/data ("final molecular charge does
#     not match"), so it is excluded rather than guessed at;
#   * the second ligand of 1HVR and 1ERE_A, which are the same molecule in another
#     copy of the asymmetric unit rather than a different active.
#
# A target needs at least two actives for a leave-one-out benchmark to score it at
# all: with one active there is no reference left once the active is removed, which
# is why `streptavidin` and `egfr` appear here and cannot be benchmarked.
#
# `trypsin` is deliberately the **five ring-amidines** and not the six amidines of
# demo/library.smi: benzylamidine is a series member rather than a co-crystallised
# ligand, and adding it was measured to *cost* power rather than add it (the pooled
# minimal detectable difference goes from 0.174 to 0.354 AUC, because the extra
# active is neither property-matched by the pool nor ranked consistently by the
# methods).  The measurement is in docs/LBVS.md §9.
#
# SMILES name target
c1ccc(cc1)C(=N)N                benzamidine             trypsin
c1ccc(cc1)C(=N)NC               benzamidine_methyl      trypsin
N=C(N)c1ccc(O)cc1               hydroxybenzamidine      trypsin
N=C(N)c1ccc(F)cc1               fluorobenzamidine       trypsin
N=C(N)c1ccccc1Cl                chloro_benzamidine      trypsin
C[C@]12CC[C@@H]3c4ccc(O)cc4CC[C@H]3[C@@H]1CC[C@@H]2O  estradiol  eralpha
CC/C(=C(\c1ccc(O)cc1)c1ccc(OCCN(C)C)cc1)c1ccccc1      OHT        eralpha
O=C1N(Cc2ccc3ccccc3c2)[C@H](Cc2ccccc2)[C@H](O)[C@@H](O)[C@@H](Cc2ccccc2)N1Cc1ccc2ccccc2c1  XK263  hiv_protease
C#Cc1cccc(Nc2ncnc3cc(OCCOC)c(OCCOC)cc23)c1            erlotinib  egfr
O=C(O)CCCC[C@@H]1SC[C@@H]2NC(=O)N[C@@H]21              biotin     streptavidin
